# steps/named-struct-exec.md, slice 3, under --walk-methods: unit_named_struct_exec_method with bump
# walked -- its bare `Counter` is a CALL(Counter's procedure, Counter) in bump's frames (§12).  bump executes
# it twice and reads Counter\n: 1, the declaration ran again.  The root wrote 5 before the call and
# reads 1 after it.  Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    n: n + 1U
return
fn: bump () size_t
    Counter
    Counter
    size_t: v 9U
    v: Counter\n
return: v
size_t: before 9U
before: Counter\n
Counter\n: 5U
size_t: got 9U
got: bump()
size_t: after 9U
after: Counter\n
int: ok 0
if: before = 0U && got = 1U && after = 1U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
